    <GaugingStation location="Fosters Bridge" name="Chater" number="31010">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Compound Crump gauging a rural, near-natural catchment with minimal artificial influences and with mixed geology.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Not drowned but possibly bypassed in very extreme floods. Theoretical rating applied across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Compound Crump profile weir. Central weir 1.054m wide, total width 6.077m.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">No major abstractions or returns - natural to within 10% at Q95.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Geology mixed, predominantly clay but contains also limestone and sandstone. Some Boulder Clay cover. Rural catchment with mixed farming, some woodland in lower catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Although not gauged to within 30% of QMED, all flows contained and remains modular." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Structure may be passed at stage above 1.5m, below AMAX3." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
